{"study_accession":"PRJNA646928","secondary_study_accession":"SRP272375","title":"Digital Gene Expression profiles analysis of patients with HCV-related hepatic fibrosis","description":"Hepatitis C virus (HCV) infection is an important etiology of chronic liver disease. Multiple possible molecular mechanisms were involved in the progression of liver fibrosis in chronically HCV-infected patients. Therefore, the further revealing novel genes for regulating liver fibrosis might provide evidence for gene diagnosis and molecular-targeted therapy. In this study, we examined the differentially expressed mRNA in plasma samples from the healthy control and patients with HCV-related liver fibrosis, in order to explore the potential predicted and therapeutic target for the development of HCV-related liver fibrosis. Overall design: Plasma samples from HCV patients with moderate to severe liver fibrosis (F3-4) and healthy control subjects (each group included 3 cases) were used for whole transcript digital gene expression (DGE) profiling sequencing.","pubmed":"33015132","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15568062","study_accession":"PRJNA646928","blood_class":"plasma_serum_cfrna","class_from":"sample","title":"HCV-related hepatic fibrosis patient 3","description":"HCV-related hepatic fibrosis patient 3","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4663399","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-09-12","attributes":[["source_name","plasma"],["tissue","Plasma"],["diagnosis","HCV with severe hepatic fibrosis (F3-4)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12247921","experiment_accession":"SRX8755820","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":18349978,"base_count":5504993400,"first_public":"2020-09-12","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM4663399: HCV-related hepatic fibrosis patient 3 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession"